// A variable is an item, declared once however many capabilities read it, and a read is
// its value.
//# build text: {home}/tests/helpers/text.ctx

// The IR is the program's and std's, with ids that change when std does: `{n}` is an id.
//# $ ctxc ir {std} -- main0.ctx
//# stdout has:
//| (var 0 "optind" "optind" {n})

// The program's variable is the only one, but for std's: std's start reads environ on Linux
// and macOS, a variable of its own. The two reads, in `a` and in `b`, are each a `cvar`.
//# $ {text} to p.ir {ctxc} ir {std} -- main0.ctx
//# exit: 0
//# $ {text} count p.ir "(var " "(var 1 \x22environ\x22 \x22environ\x22" "(cvar {n} 0)"
//# [windows] stdout:
//| 1
//| 0
//| 2
//# [posix] stdout:
//| 2
//| 1
//| 2
